I take my bag and go to the shop.
It is a small shop near my building.
I go near the counter and speak with the shopkeeper.
"Bhaiya, namaste," I say.
"Namaste madam, what do you need?" he asks.
"First, I need half a kilo of poha," I indicate.
He says yes and weighs the poha.
"Then, please give me a small packet of peanuts too."
He places those items on the counter.
"Do you need anything else?" he asks.
"No, only this."
"How many rupees?" I ask.
"Sixty rupees," the shopkeeper says.
I give him the rupees.
He gives me a receipt.
After that, I put all the items in my bag.
Now I need fresh vegetables for the Kande Pohe meal.
I leave the shop and walk towards the vegetable cart.
